          "title": "You'll want to know: 生意",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "生意 — shēngyi — \"business; trade\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "每年这个时候月饼的生意最好 měinián zhège shíhou yuèbǐng de shēngyi zuì hǎo — Every year at this time the mooncake trade is at its best."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "生意 (shēngyi) is built from 生 'life' and 意 'intent', both inherited from Middle Chinese, srjaeng and 'iH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to grow' and the second 'the will'. How the pair came to mean business is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
